  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Balloon A and balloon B contain atoms of the same ideal gas. The volume of balloon A is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span> and the volume of balloon B is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"40\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span>. The pressure in balloon A is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\"></span> Pa and the pressure in balloon B is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"10\"></span> Pa. After the balloons are joined by a tube of negligible volume, the pressure in the balloons is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"6.0\"></span> Pa. The temperature of the balloons is unchanged. What is the combined volume of the balloons after they have been joined by the tube?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"90\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"100\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"180\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\"></span> m<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{3}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
